Development, inequality, and international Political-Economy (@development-inequality-and-international-political-economy: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_34KW7KS9CP6TSBK63H7JJNX64S
This material investigates uneven development, structural change, inequality, trade, investment, international production, and the distribution of economic and political power. It connects industrialisation, technological capabilities, labour, institutions, resource use, dependency, and cooperation across regions. Compare explanations through historical cases and current observations, identifying the scale and conditions of each claim. Link global supply systems and local productive capacity to the people and arrangements through which their benefits, costs, and decisions are distributed.

**Parent:** [Political-Economy](../Political-Economy.lingua#r_2WPG1Y767BM24Z0K4BY6Y6T62W).
